			<div class="content" id="post-content-1177069">
									

<ol>
<li>Well, Of Course. Am I not <em>Bland</em>?</li>
<li>No, it's just the a convergence of things - Agatha isn't a common name, but it's not unique; you'd have to ask the creator of Agatha Rights if the character was even inspired by GG. Mad Science has been cool since Dr. Frankenstein installed the first set of bolts in a neck.</li>
</ol>
<p>I understand where you're coming from, though. This is simply a cultural saturation thing - a &quot;common elements coming together&quot; sort of thing to form something that seems similar to something else that is known is a normal psychological thing. I fell prey to a while back with something else.</p>

