    <div class="post-container" id="fpc-1259311">
                      
		<div class="post" id="post-1259311">
		<div class="long">
			<div class="head">
									<div class="options">
						<a href="javascript:;" onclick="togglePostFold(event,1259311)" class="btn btn-default btn-small btn-sm">Fold</a>
					</div>
								<div class="title" id="post-title-1259311">
																		
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dreverettmann" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(323946); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=323946&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608930883" alt="DrEverettMann" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=323946)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dreverettmann" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(323946); return false;" >DrEverettMann</a></span> <span class="odate time_1316094551 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">15 Sep 2011 13:49</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1259311">
									

<p>For the first, consider that the first laboratory was basically just a shack some guy set up in the woods. That shack is where those equations were derived. Afterwards, the organization grew slowly. This might have been their only parcel of land in a suitably out-of-the-way location for a while. Read the story again. The Foundation didn't crop up overnight. And, of course, it <em>is</em> the place where it all started. They have a vested interest in keeping the area secure and watching for any changes. Anything they might have missed the first time. And it's kind of a legacy site. Not even the O5s are immune to sentiment.</p>
<p>For the second, that neatness, that improbable wholeness, is the whole point of this. That's what makes it horrifying.</p>

							</div>

								
					
